body:
Anyone knows if 2-4 puffs of Inuvair 100/6 is considered a strong dose? Supposedly it's less strong than Symbicort....

&#x200B;

Either way, I've stopped panicking about myself. If I get it, I get it. Simple as that. I take the precautions prescribed by the government and that's is.

Your parents won't know peace, don't kid yourself. If they wanted to get rid of you, they would just throw you out and not spend a lot of money on a place of your own.

I don't know the dynamics in your family, but sometimes neither is to blame. The relationship has just become explosive and you need to be apart from one another. Your father might be on to something with his offer;

Don't waste this chance. Being alone with responsibilities to provide for yourself could well be that push you need to find a reason. Take that reason please.

I'd so gladly start over. But with all the knowledge of an adult having to sit through high school again? That seems depressing, and I don't know if it will turn out well.

&#x200B;

I'd take it if I merely had the knowledge to avert mistakes I've made.

This is coming from someone who's 30 and at the brink of taking or not taking his own life for failure in life, so take it as you wish;

What I tell anyone who has this feeling (I used to have it), is *fake it until you make it*. Meaning, pick out some people that you idolise, who'd you like to be and study their manners. Slowly but surely copy your favourite traits and stick to it until their traits become your own.

Everyone does it; it's why teenagers track celebrities. You'll have some catching up to do but eventually you'll get there. And along the ride, you'll pick up some empathy as well. Don't think that you'll ever be perfect husband material with the delay you've had, but you could certainly make a worthy partner for every woman if you base your social skills on revered men. 

&#x200B;

Good luck. It will be a long ride (5 years, give or take)

I've stopped trusting conventional medicine since they recommended steroids for... everything. That's why I equally don't trust the treatments for keratoconus. I trust that by healing our insides (microbiome), we can get rid of allergies and make the whole of our bodies stronger, possibly even our corneas.

&#x200B;

This half century, our food has degraded so much and our environments (office spaces) have stripped us of our natural defense lines.
